.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt RADIO-SETUP.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm radio-setup.sh
.Nd configure a MANET node after first boot or a configuration change
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the node configuration, assigns radio roles, writes network and
service configuration, installs required packages and starts runtime services.
Run it as root with power and an internet uplink connected.
It may reboot the node to apply interface names or boot configuration.
The first-boot service repeats setup after a required reboot.
.Pp
The command takes no options.
It can be run again after editing
.Pa /etc/mesh.conf
or to retry incomplete provisioning.
Only one setup run proceeds at a time.
Failed steps are recorded; a run with recorded failures leaves the node
marked incomplete.
After successful setup, staged operator scripts run in a separate service.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/mesh.conf
Node and mesh settings.
.It Pa /var/log/radio-setup.log
Appended setup output and shell trace.
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-provision.state
Provisioning phase and result.
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-provision.failures
Failed setup steps.
.It Pa /var/lib/radio-setup.done
Successful completion marker.
.It Pa /var/lib/mesh_if , /var/lib/halow_if , /var/lib/ap_interface
Assigned radio roles.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after success, when another setup run holds the lock, or when a
required reboot has been requested.
A nonzero status indicates a setup error.
Use the provisioning status command to confirm completion after a reboot.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Retry setup after restoring the internet uplink:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo radio-setup.sh
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr manet-provision-status.sh 8 ,
.Xr manet-user-scripts.sh 8 ,
.Xr verify-bridge.sh 8
